    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0438" n="434" xml:id="pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">398.115 Tung or Wood Oil/13: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spiker</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-29T15:00:00+08:00">July 29, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 29—10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>177. My July 26, 9 p.m. Japanese Consul General states that Japanese authorities
                    concerned are now discussing possible means for shipment from Hankow of wood oil
                    belonging to the three interested American companies.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, Shanghai. Shanghai repeat to Tokyo by
                    airmail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spiker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
